59,3,,status,Misaki,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
60,3,1,talk,Mio,,Option A feels safe. I know what I owe in winter. No surprises.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,"Option A has no upfront cost. The annual settle is a risk, but I can budget for it.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Rin,,Option A means one big calculation a year. That is manageable. I can do that.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,"Option A ignores the four-to-one disparity. It is a compromise, not a solution.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Misaki,,Option A removes the monthly trigger. No monthly bill means no monthly fight.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Mio,,"@Shunichi, but the disparity is in the shared heating. If I pay a fixed rate, I am covered.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Mio, exactly. The fixed rate covers the variance. I don't need to know the exact kilowatt-hour.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Rin,,"@Ryuji, I agree. The template trial showed that exactness is a trap. I want simplicity.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Rin, simplicity is good, but it hides the waste. The monitors show we are burning money.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Shunichi, the waste is a habit, not a billing error. The cooler notice shows we avoid the bill, not the heat.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Mio,,"Option B is too expensive. 34,000 yen per room is impossible for me.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,Option B is out. The upfront cost is a barrier I cannot cross. I need to stay liquid.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Rin,,Option B requires new hardware. I don't want to install meters. I want to stop doing math.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,"Option B is the only mathematically fair one. But if you can't afford it, it is useless.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Misaki,,Option B creates a new point of contention. Who reads the meters? Who disputes the reading?,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Mio,,Option C is too volatile. February would be a nightmare. I need stability.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,"Option C is a gamble. I cannot plan my year if the bill swings 20,000 yen.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Rin,,Option C means I am the accountant again. I refuse. I need a system that doesn't need me.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,Option C is the status quo. It is the problem. We are here to change it.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Misaki,,Option C is the path to the cooler notice. We will avoid the bill and suffer in the cold.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
